Additional Use Grant: You may make production use of the Licensed Work
 only to inspect and protect HTTP applications that you or your
 Affiliates operate on systems under your direct control (self-hosted
 deployment).  "Affiliate" means an entity that controls, is controlled
 by, or is under common control with you.

 Usage Threshold: The production use grant above applies only if your
 organization and all Affiliates collectively do not exceed either of
 the following limits:

  (a) 200,000,000 (two hundred million) HTTP requests processed by
      all instances of the Licensed Work in any rolling calendar
      month (the thirty-day period ending at the moment of
      measurement); OR

  (b) 32 (thirty-two) nginx worker processes running the Licensed
      Work across all instances at any point in time.

 Exceeding either limit requires a commercial license from Licensor.
 If you first exceed a limit, you have thirty (30) days to obtain
 such a license or cease production use.

 Infrastructure Provider Restriction: Notwithstanding the foregoing,
 you may not use the Licensed Work in production if your organization
 or any Affiliate derives twenty percent (20%) or more of its total
 annual gross revenue from providing internet infrastructure services
 to third parties, including but not limited to: content delivery
 networks (CDN), cloud computing platforms, web hosting services,
 managed server hosting, internet exchange points, or internet transit
 services.  This restriction applies regardless of whether the Licensed
 Work is deployed solely to protect your own systems rather than those
 of your customers.  Organizations that meet this criterion must obtain
 a commercial license from Licensor.

 You may not use the Licensed Work for a WAF Service.  A "WAF Service"
 is any offering made available to third parties (other than your
 employees and contractors) where the principal value is inspecting,
 filtering, scoring, or blocking HTTP traffic for those third parties
 using the Licensed Work on infrastructure you operate, and where those
 third parties do not themselves receive a copy of the Licensed Work to
 run on infrastructure they control.  Without limitation, this includes
 software-as-a-service, managed or hosted WAF, multi-tenant reverse-proxy
 filtering sold by subscription, and similar remote-access models.

 Development, testing, benchmarking, and other non-production use
 remain governed by the standard Terms below.  If you need rights that
 this License does not grant (including operating a WAF Service, or
 exceeding the Usage Threshold, or qualifying as an Infrastructure
 Provider), you must obtain a separate commercial license from Licensor.

